/* File: stories/politician/screenplay.fountain
   Shooting script draft 1, written on Leonard's request before the bible lock.
   Shot notes: [[SHOT | seconds | size and angle | movement | note]]. Scene ids S01..S10, shot ids SH010.. per scene (repo pipeline).
   Pending (bible, open items): bills on top of the contract; the miscount comes from the uncounted warning shot; "Get in."
   Proposed in this draft: the scope with face boxes (S08 SH030). */

FADE IN:

.EXT. CITIES - VARIOUS - DAY TO SUNSET #S01#

[[SH010 | 4 | WIDE, high | Handheld, phone-camera feel | Riots open the film (Leonard)]]
A crowd fills an avenue from wall to wall. Above the heads, signs with the same old face: devil horns drawn on, the eyes crossed out in red, one printout of him hanging from a noose.

NEWS ANCHORS (V.O.)
(overlapping, many accents)
...a fourth day of losses on the markets... ...fuel up again overnight...

[[SH020 | 2 | INSERT | Locked-off | ]]
A cardboard sign. His face. A red X over each eye.

[[SH030 | 3 | MEDIUM | Locked-off | ]]
A gas station. A worker on a ladder slides new numbers into the price board. Higher. A line of cars behind him.

[[SH040 | 3 | WIDE, long lens | Locked-off | ]]
A highway out of the city, jammed. Mattresses tied on car roofs. Children's faces at the windows.

[[SH050 | 4 | WIDE, long lens | Handheld | Distance: nothing explicit]]
A police line. Hands pull a POLICEMAN into the crowd by his vest. Another officer drags him back. A pistol rises above the heads and fires. The police fire back. Everyone scatters.

[[SH060 | 3 | WIDE | Locked-off | ]]
A bottle of fire bursts against a police truck. The truck burns.

[[SH070 | 3 | EXTREME WIDE | Slow pan | ]]
Sunset. The skyline, columns of smoke, sirens far away.

[[SH080 | 6 | MEDIUM CLOSE | Locked-off | ]]
A REPORTER, glamorous, every hair in place, on a rooftop. Smoke behind her.

REPORTER
His location is still unknown. Authorities are warning the locals that any harm to this man will have serious repercussions.

SMASH CUT TO:

.EXT. ROAD INTO A TOWN - DAY #S02#

[[SH010 | 3 | EXTREME WIDE | Locked-off | Hard cut to silence]]
Silence. The sun hits the rooftops of a dry, dusty town.

[[SH020 | 3 | MEDIUM | Locked-off | ]]
A cat lies in the shadow of an abandoned building, on the edge of a crumbled concrete wall. Heat rises from the asphalt.

[[SH030 | 3 | LOW, road level | Locked-off, car passes over camera | The speeding car (Leonard)]]
A car tears over the camera at full speed. Tires screech. It slides to a rough stop.

[[SH040 | 4 | MEDIUM, through windshield | Locked-off | ]]
The OLD MAN behind the wheel, an expensive shirt dark with sweat, slowly raises his head and looks ahead, frightened. On the dashboard a wobble head keeps nodding. A BRIEFCASE on the passenger seat.

[[SH050 | 3 | POV | Dolly zoom | Vertigo effect (Leonard)]]
The main road, straight into the center of the town. It stretches away from him.

[[SH060 | 3 | MEDIUM | Two whip pans, left and right | ]]
Left: the side road is sealed by a wall. Right: another wall. Desert beyond both.

[[SH070 | 2 | INSERT | Locked-off | ]]
The rear-view mirror. An empty road. Nobody.

[[SH080 | 2 | INSERT | Locked-off | ]]
The fuel needle rests on the edge of E.

[[SH090 | 4 | CLOSE | Locked-off | ]]
Sweat runs from his temple. He breathes in, and gently presses the accelerator. The car rolls toward the town.

.EXT. TOWN - MAIN STREET - DAY #S03#

[[SH010 | 5 | WIDE | Slow track with the car | ]]
The car crawls between tall, cheap apartment blocks. Laundry, satellite dishes, shutters half down. Right after lunch: nobody outside. From open windows the same news echoes from television to television.

REPORTER (V.O.)
(from the televisions)
...any harm to this man...

[[SH020 | 6 | MEDIUM, passenger side | Locked-off | ]]
He glances at the briefcase.

OLD MAN
We'll get there, don't worry... Wait till they see what I was able to-- what--? No, no no no...

The engine pops.

[[SH030 | 4 | WIDE | Locked-off | Part 2 beat (Leonard)]]
The car slows and stops at the edge of a square. A beep: the fuel light. He twists the key. Nothing. The last clap of the engine echoes off the buildings.

[[SH040 | 5 | MEDIUM CLOSE | Handheld, gentle | ]]
OLD MAN
Not here, no...

He peeks around. Empty. He takes the briefcase and gets out, leaving the door open.

[[SH050 | 3 | EXTREME WIDE, high | Locked-off | ]]
The deserted square. A small figure walks away from the car.

.EXT. TOWN - STREETS - DAY #S04#

[[SH010 | 4 | MEDIUM | Handheld, tracking beside him | We stay with him (Leonard, Q12)]]
He walks fast, the briefcase held against his chest, trying not to make a sound. His breath gets heavier. His eyes check every doorway.

[[SH020 | 3 | MEDIUM WIDE | Handheld | ]]
On his left, a small group of men at a doorway, minding their own business. He looks right--

[[SH030 | 6 | TWO SHOT | Handheld | ]]
--and walks straight into a big, robust FAT PERSON. They look at each other. The old man is terrified and tries not to show it. The fat person is curious. He can't place him. Then his eyes widen.

FAT PERSON
This can't be. Is it really you?

[[SH040 | 4 | CLOSE | Handheld | ]]
The old man covers his face with his hand.

OLD MAN
I don't know who you think I am. I don't know you!

[[SH050 | 5 | MEDIUM | Handheld | ]]
FAT PERSON
It IS you. What are you doing here, all alone? Nobody around to baby-sit you?

Behind him, his FRIEND takes out a phone and starts texting.

[[SH060 | 7 | CLOSE TWO SHOT | Handheld, tight | ]]
The fat person grabs him by the collar.

FAT PERSON
You ruined so many lives. Is that what you do with our tax money? Give me one reason why I shouldn't rip your guts open right now, in front of everyone.

[[SH070 | 2 | WIDE, low | Locked-off | ]]
Above them, faces appear at the windows.

[[SH080 | 4 | MEDIUM | Handheld | ]]
The old man shrinks and slides out of the grip. The fat person lets him go.

FRIEND
Are you stupid!? Go after him. It's really him!

.EXT. TOWN - STREETS - CONTINUOUS #S05#

[[SH010 | 4 | MEDIUM | Handheld, backing in front of him | ]]
He walks faster, wipes the sweat from his forehead. Voices rise from the buildings, louder and louder.

VOICES
It's him? Oh god, it's really him!

[[SH020 | 4 | WIDE, long lens | Handheld | ]]
Behind him, the two friends follow, walking, then faster. People come out of doorways and join them.

[[SH030 | 3 | WIDE | Handheld, running | ]]
He runs. A whole crowd runs after him, faster than he is.

[[SH040 | 3 | MEDIUM | Handheld, running | Pending: bills on top of the contract]]
The briefcase snaps open. Large bills burst out and fly in the wind, raining onto the crowd.

[[SH050 | 4 | WIDE | Handheld | ]]
The crowd drops to the ground, grabbing at the bills. He fumbles with the case, can't close it, and throws it away.

[[SH060 | 3 | CLOSE | Handheld, running | ]]
VOICE (O.S.)
Don't let him get away!!!

Running, he pulls out his phone. Sweat on his thumb. The screen won't unlock. It does. He dials.

[[SH070 | 6 | CLOSE | Handheld, running | ]]
OLD MAN
(into the phone)
It's me! I have the money! The car broke down, I'm on foot, come get me, fast! I'm slightly south from where we were supposed to meet, the add--

A rock hits him between the phone and his ear.

[[SH080 | 3 | WIDE | Handheld | ]]
He falls and rolls onto the sidewalk. Blood runs down his face. The yelling closes in.

.EXT. TOWN - STREET - CONTINUOUS #S06#

[[SH010 | 4 | MEDIUM, low | Locked-off | Warning shot: one]]
A gunshot. Everyone freezes. On the ground, he holds a small pistol up at the sky.

OLD MAN
STAY BACK!!!

[[SH020 | 4 | MEDIUM | Handheld | ]]
He points it at the crowd. They take a step back.

OLD MAN
Don't get close! Go away!

[[SH030 | 5 | WIDE | Slow push in | ]]
Some of them back away. The tough ones step forward. They don't run. They walk toward him, slowly, without fear.

[[SH040 | 6 | MEDIUM, his side | Handheld | Distance on the falls: nothing explicit]]
He shoots. A man drops. He shoots again. Another drops. The rest break into a sprint. He keeps firing, lips moving.

OLD MAN
(under his breath)
...three... four... five.

[[SH050 | 4 | CLOSE | Locked-off | Pending: miscount from the uncounted warning shot (Leonard, Q13)]]
He stops. One left. He turns the pistol to his own temple and shuts his eyes.

Click.

[[SH060 | 2 | CLOSE | Locked-off | ]]
He opens his eyes and looks at the gun. The crowd reaches him.

.EXT. TOWN - STREET - MOMENTS LATER #S07#

[[SH010 | 4 | EXTREME WIDE, high | Locked-off | Seen from afar (Leonard)]]
From far above, the small mob closes around him. He disappears inside it. Fists and kicks rise and fall.

[[SH020 | 4 | WIDE | Locked-off | ]]
A rope around his ankles. They haul him up, upside down, from a street light.

[[SH030 | 3 | CLOSE, upside down | Locked-off | ]]
His face, swollen like a balloon, blood dripping from his ear and his lips. With effort, he opens one eye.

[[SH040 | 2 | POV, upside down | Locked-off | ]]
A man raises a metal pipe.

[[SH050 | 3 | MEDIUM | Locked-off | A swing or two (Leonard). Impact on the body, off the face]]
The pipe swings into his body. Again.

[[SH060 | 3 | MEDIUM WIDE | Locked-off | No splatter, no brains (Leonard)]]
The man lifts the pipe high for the last blow. A crack from the sky. He drops. The pipe rings on the asphalt. The crowd steps back.

.EXT. SKY ABOVE THE TOWN / INT. HELICOPTER - CONTINUOUS #S08#

[[SH010 | 3 | EXTREME WIDE, long lens | Locked-off | Tone shift: Clancy, hint of Kojima (Leonard, Q12). Model: research]]
A sleek black helicopter holds still, high above the rooftops. No markings. The side door open.

[[SH020 | 3 | CLOSE | Locked-off, cabin vibration | ]]
In the door, ROGER, harnessed in, cheek on the stock of a long rifle. He is smiling.

[[SH030 | 4 | SCOPE POV | Steady, stabilized | PROPOSED: the tech that exists but nobody sees]]
The street below through his scope. A thin box frames every face: red. One box, upside down under the street light, is green. The crosshair moves from red box to red box.

[[SH040 | 5 | WIDE, from the street, long lens | Locked-off | Distance and dust: nothing explicit]]
Cracks from the sky. People fall. The rest run. Some fall while they run.

[[SH050 | 3 | MEDIUM | Locked-off | ]]
Behind Roger, seated, headset on: the BUSINESS LADY.

BUSINESS LADY
That's enough Roger.

[[SH060 | 3 | CLOSE | Locked-off | ]]
Roger's face, for an instant: a child whose candy was taken. Then his face goes blank. He shifts his aim.

[[SH070 | 2 | SCOPE POV, then WIDE | Cut | ]]
The crosshair on the rope. A crack. The rope snaps.

.EXT. TOWN - STREET - CONTINUOUS #S09#

[[SH010 | 4 | MEDIUM | Handheld | ]]
He drops onto the asphalt. He yells, curled up. A dark stain spreads down his trousers.

[[SH020 | 4 | HIS POV, then CLOSE | Handheld | ]]
Around him, the dead lie in the street, bills stuck to the asphalt between them. His face changes. The fear leaves it.

[[SH030 | 3 | MEDIUM | Locked-off | ]]
He spits on the nearest body.

[[SH040 | 5 | WIDE | Locked-off | ]]
He gets up and limps toward the briefcase in the middle of the street. Above him the helicopter comes down. The rotor wash blows the loose bills across the bodies.

[[SH050 | 3 | INSERT | Locked-off | Pending: the contract]]
He opens the case, reaches into the pocket inside the lid and takes out a folder.

[[SH060 | 3 | WIDE | Locked-off | ]]
The helicopter touches down. The BUSINESS LADY steps out, low under the rotors.

[[SH070 | 4 | MEDIUM | Locked-off | His line (Leonard)]]
OLD MAN
What took you so long? I don't pay your ass for nothing.

[[SH080 | 6 | TWO SHOT | Locked-off | Pending: "Get in." Her silence answers him]]
She doesn't answer. She holds out her hand. He gives her the folder. She opens it: a page of signatures and stamps. She reads it, then looks at him.

BUSINESS LADY
Get in.

[[SH090 | 2 | MEDIUM | Locked-off | ]]
He climbs in after her.

.EXT. SKY - CONTINUOUS #S10#

[[SH010 | 8 | EXTREME WIDE | Locked-off | Final image: the helicopter going away (Leonard)]]
The helicopter lifts off, banks over the rooftops and goes away into the sky, until it is gone.

> CUT TO BLACK.
